279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 76 0 R
/T (Ans: Feature extraction and segmentation algorithms rely on detecting differences in intensity \(edges, boundaries, textures\) between regions. Histogram equalization enhances contrast so these intensity differences become more pronounced and consistent, making features and object boundaries easier for algorithms to detect accurately, especially in images that were originally poorly lit or low-contrast.)
/E (Ans: Feature extraction and segmentation algorithms rely on detecting differences in intensity \(edges, boundaries, textures\) between regions. Histogram equalization enhances contrast so these intensity differences become more pronounced and consistent, making features and object boundaries easier for algorithms to detect accurately, especially in images that were originally poorly lit or low-contrast.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
