577 0 obj
<<
/Title (Q4. What is Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization \(CLAHE\)? How does it differ from standard Histogram Equalization?)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 678 0 R
/First 679 0 R
/Last 679 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 440 0 R
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ans: Feature extraction and segmentation algorithms rely on detecting differences in intensity \(edges, boundaries, textures\) between regions. Histogram equalization enhances contrast so these intensity differences become more pronounced and consistent, making features and object boundaries easier for algorithms to detect accurately, especially in images that were originally poorly lit or low-contrast.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 440 0 R
>>
endobj
